From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: the DFlash2 draft knobs (TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_*)

ai-engine 39304587f with 0f4b0ed85's window parse. Adds the knob module and the surfaces it
drives: onepass, down4, mlpsplit, edge, noisy, noise, keepwin and cuts, the KEEPWIN window and
its restart/ring bookkeeping, the q4 fp32 matmul family the draft head needs, and the drafter
tests. Drafting only: no reply path reads these.

Receipt (ai-engine): the drafter is worth 61.08 against 58.41 tok/s at one stream on the padded
build, and the draft-chain confidence sweep at four streams measured 0.5 to 90.68/90.63,
0.7 (default) to 94.14/94.13, 0.85 to 91.54/91.13, so the threshold stays where it is. Every
knob defaults off; the drafter itself is a serve flag, not a knob.

Gate: applies on the pin stack; check-native-cuda-host green; whole-tree fmt green; lean
base-vs-head 0 new; fatbins green.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0003: the three DFlash2 lines it carried - the dflash_ovn test import, prefillStart's snapshots.resumeDrafter and draftBlock's dflash.located - which name this patch's own code
- 0024: windowBytes reads DRAFT_KEEPWIN before the drafter, and the host engines set `drafter`
- 0033: the DOWN4 check's capture no longer shadows the rng binding
- 0041: cuda_q4.Kernels.module is set, and dflash_load keeps the pin's header and short-read checks and sets Drafter.tap_rows
- 0058: the selector reads DRAFT_EDGE, _NOISE and _BETA, which the port left unread
- 0059: df_sumw's kernel-contract record, which the port brought the kernel without

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: the eight TF_GLM_OVN_DRAFT_* knobs and TF_GLM_DFLASH2_WIN are .glm rows (flag, u64, signed_real/positive_real/real, and DRAFT_CUTS as the table's one text kind, .path); dflash_ovn reads them through cuda.ovn.real/text, and the old float() parser goes.
- TF_GLM_DFLASH2_WIN: dflash.parseWin becomes dflash.windowSetting, an environment.read of a u64 row capped at WIN (2048) with space trimming, the same accepted forms; its test reads the row.
- c632a57f0 made dflash.confidence() a registry read that can fail: draftBlock's DRAFT_CUTS line takes `try dflash.confidence()`, and keeps one line so cuda_lanes.zig stays at v1.2.7's 600.
- dflash_load.zig (v1.2.7 added .checkpoint_digest and .bits to the Drafter literal): the knob fields join that literal.
- cuda_env_test.zig lists TF_GLM_DFLASH2_WIN among GLM's own readers (a bounded count).
- dflash.ingestsNone is left out: its only caller was fold 0010's drafterIdle (pairing beside a drafter), which this re-seat defers (DECISIONS.md, fold 0010).
- source: work/fold/0007-draft-knobs.patch

